\section{Reputation Estimates Tracking and Role Switching}
\subsection{Definitions}
Theoretical definition of personal utility:
\[
U_i(\pi_i) = \sum_{s \in S} p(s) u_i(s, \pi_i(s))
\]  
Theoretical definition of reputation:
$$ R_i(\pi_i) = \gamma \sum_{j \in G\setminus\{i\}} \sum_{s \in S} u_j(\pi_i(s))$$

In the simulation environment, at any time $t$, each agent $i$ keeps track of the following estimates:
\begin{itemize}
% \item Personal utility estimates: 

\item Personal estimate of agent $j$'s utility to $i$:
$$P^{(0)}_{j,i} = u_j^{(0)}(s, \pi_i(s))$$
$$P_{j,i}^{(t+1)} 
    = (1-\alpha)\cdot P_{j,i}^{(t)} + 
    \alpha \cdot u^{(t)}_j(\pi_i(s))$$
\item Reputation estimate of agent $j$: 
$$R_{j,i}^{(0)} = 0, \qquad \forall j \neq i$$
$$R_{j,i}^{(t+1)} 
    = R_{j,i}^{(t)} + \left(P_{j,i}^{(t+1)} - P_{j,i}^{(t)}\right)$$

\end{itemize}

Need to reconcile the true reputation with the reputation estimates. 
