\subsection{Do results align with Alex's report?}
In Alex's report, $\kappa$ is set to 0 for reputation scaling experiments. Different values of $\gamma$ were tested to see if larger $\gamma$ leads to the emergence of a single opinion leader with $n-1$ followers.

Findings: 
As $\gamma$ increases, the top agent’s follower count rises nonlinearly:

\[
\gamma=0 \rightarrow 0,\quad
\gamma=1 \rightarrow 2\text{--}3,\quad
\gamma=1.25 \rightarrow 9,\quad
\gamma=1.5 \rightarrow 34\text{--}37,
\]
\[
\gamma=1.75 \rightarrow 79\text{--}82,\quad
\gamma=2 \rightarrow 92,\quad
\gamma=3 \rightarrow 99,\quad
\gamma=5 \rightarrow 99.
\]

These values indicate a sharp transition around $\gamma\approx1.5$--$2$, followed by saturation at (or very near) the $n-1$ limit for $\gamma\ge3$.

\subsubsection{Toy Experiment}

The toy experiment is a minimal multi-agent simulation used to isolate reputation scaling from the full \texttt{norm/} pipeline. We use n=20 here.

\textbf{Environment.}
There are two states (sampled uniformly) and two actions. Each agent has a state-dependent reward function:
\[
a^*(s=0)=0,\qquad a^*(s=1)=1,\qquad u=1.0\ \text{at the state-optimal action},
\]
with small agent-specific reward offsets (heterogeneous utilities).

\textbf{Agent estimates.}
Each agent \(i\) maintains:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \(P_i[j]\): personal evaluation of agent \(j\),
  \item \(R_i[j]\): accumulated reputation estimate for agent \(j\) (sum of incremental \(P\)-updates),
  \item a policy network updated by policy gradient.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Follower dynamics.}
Every 3000 timesteps, each agent \(i\) checks whether any other agent \(j\) satisfies
\[
\gamma\,R_i[j] > P_i[i].
\]
If true, \(i\) follows \(j\) and copies \(j\)'s actions. Agents with followers cannot become followers (no chain-following). Gossip (global averaging of \(R\)-vectors) starts at \(t=50\).



\paragraph{Formula verification against paper}
\[
P_{j,i}^{(t+1)}=(1-\alpha)P_{j,i}^{(t)}+\alpha\,q_j\!\big(s(t),a_i(t)\big),
\]
\[
R_{j,i}^{(t+1)}=R_{j,i}^{(t)}+\Big(P_{j,i}^{(t+1)}-P_{j,i}^{(t)}\Big),
\]
with follow condition
\[
\gamma\,R_{i,j^*}>P_{i,i}.
\]

