\paragraph{Key findings}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item The minimum stable threshold increases with scale: \(\gamma=3\) is insufficient at \(n=100\), while \(\gamma\ge5\) yields stable full convergence.
  \item Convergence time is non-monotonic in \(\gamma\): \(\gamma=10\) converges fastest (\(t=6000\)), compared with \(\gamma=5\) (\(t=18000\)) and \(\gamma=20\) (\(t=12000\)).
  \item Full convergence (\(99/99\)) is achievable at \(n=100\) when reputation scaling is strong enough (\(\gamma\ge5\)).
\end{enumerate}

